{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-information-theoretic-time","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:information-theoretic-time","kind":"definition","title":"Information-Theoretic Time","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-reeb-operations-per-planck","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-ordering-jet-compatibility"],"tags":["information-theory","planck-time","discrete-time","statistical-mechanics","reeb-flow","julia-set"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.informationTheoreticTime","text":"information-theoretic-time.md","leanSource":"information-theoretic-time.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:information-theoretic-time\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe with braiding-induced ordering <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\prec_c</code> (<a href=\"#prop:ordering-jet-compatibility\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/direct-limit\">ordering–jet compatibility</a>). Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f_q(z) = z^2 + c(q)</code> be the Julia set iteration on the exceptional divisor.</p>\n<p>The <strong>information-theoretic time</strong> at substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> is the cumulative Reeb operation count:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{T}(q)  :=  \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} 1\n  =  N</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N</code> is the total number of iterations of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f_q</code> applied since a reference configuration <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}_0</code>. Each iteration advances the admissible ordering by one step. The count <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{T}</code> determines the position in the braiding-induced ordering <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\prec_c</code> propagated through the jet tower.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/information-theoretic-time.md","heading":"Definition","number":"22.2.3","page":"b/def-information-theoretic-time","qa":{"counts":{"pass":81,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":65},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.informationTheoreticTime","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/information-theoretic-time.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
